WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.680
In 2022, bird flu swept through
egg farms across the United States.

2
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.480
More than 43 million
egg-laying hens were lost.

3
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.980
Fewer hens meant fewer eggs for sale,

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.440
whatever the price.

5
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.190
Yet in an ordinary year,

6
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:18.540
farmers send more to market
whenever the price climbs.

7
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.110
That is a different kind of change.

8
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.400
So why do farmers grow
more when prices rise,

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.470
and what makes them grow
less at every price?

10
00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.170
In this mission, you'll build
a supply curve and learn

11
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.070
the determinants of supply.

12
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.860
Then you'll add a tax
and change input prices

13
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.980
in the graph lab, and
predict what the curve does.

14
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.970
Your mission: explain what moves
a producer along the curve,

15
00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.810
and what moves the curve itself.
